    "created_at": "2024-12-10T02:52:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-10T02:52:21Z",
    "body": "It's not entirely my area of expertise, but it seems to me the `actualBoudingBox[Left|Right]` properties are supposed to read the rendered glyphs xMin and xMax values. In most fonts these are undefined for U+0020 so it makes sense leading and trailing spaces aren't part of the bounding box. \r\nEvery browser agrees that they are part of the advance width however, the one reported by `TextMetrics.width`, since they do have an advanceWidth defined. \r\n\r\nIn [this fiddle](https://jsfiddle.net/k1zwLfxg/) I created a small font where the glyph for U+0020 has an actual box defined, and we can see that neither Chrome nor Firefox do trim the input.\r\n\r\nAs for the `\\r\\n` case it seems all do agree it should become two spaces: https://jsfiddle.net/4wm8defc/",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
